public issue or PR text.","Don't merge."],"goal":"One PR that closes GitHub issue #143 (severity calibration, failure model in specs (AC8), and a good-enough bar for docs in light mode), ready and unmerged, with \"Closes #143\" in the PR body."},"mandateAssessment":{"evidence":"The design addresses all three #143 scope items, keeps the proposed edits within reviewer instructions, spec validation and templates, and light-run documentation review, and avoids the larger changes owned by #142 and #144. It records agent decisions and calls for an unmerged PR.","outcome":"PASS"},"outcome":"FAIL","output":{"bytes":1332,"format":"json","hash":"sha256:c7f8d39bc5a9e47e6bd72c459a6d19fdffcaf3aee15cda1280aab6e2c12ae13b"},"receipt":{"bytes":1369,"format":"json","hash":"sha256:c53a24b3da0ca99bdb1001746e67c08f7315183d1ebcacf88ba1bbbde8f6ccb2"},"reviewContract":"sha256:33046a7b328e55cf539c21c18523876347b7f41d2434ad14c6d2017a4fe115ee","runId":"tb-convergence-severity-calibration-start-1","subject":"sha256:f996bf02ac7cc933e79d036daf5ca0b0f951f16910d6657cb9551ced1698538b","summary":"The design is coherent and bounded, but its treatment of resumed runs contradicts a settled requirement. That exception needs resolution before design approval."}